<title>UK: B.A.T Industries gain as Kessler resigns.</title>
<headline>B.A.T Industries gain as Kessler resigns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in B.A.T Industries gained on Tuesday after David Kessler, a vocal anti-smoking advocate, said he would resign as U.S. Food and Drug Administration Commissioner once a successor was named, dealers said.</p>
<p>B.A.T Industries shares rose 9p to 468p by 0852 GMT following a strong performance by U.S. tobacco shares in New York overnight.</p>
<p>Philip Morris jumped $3-1/8 to $105-1/2 following the news that Kessler intended to leave his post.</p>
<p>&quot;Kessler has been seen as being a bit harsh on the tobacco industry in the past,&quot; one marketmaker said.</p>
<p>Imperial Tobacco fell 1/2p to 376p. --London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
